  "raw_text": "No. A single customer complaint may indicate a problem in one interaction, but it is usually insufficient to conclude that a worker is **generally rude**.\n\nTo support a broader conclusion, consider:\n\n- Whether other complaints or observations show a pattern\n- The specificity and credibility of the complaint\n- The worker’s account and any witnesses or recordings\n- The context, including misunderstandings or unusual circumstances\n- Prior performance and conduct records\n\nThe complaint should be documented and investigated, but any response should distinguish between addressing a specific incident and labeling the worker’s overall character or behavior.",
